#################
### Prompt start: \[\e]133;A\e\\\]
# \[ starts an enclosure within which characters produce no visible output
# \e] is an escape character for Operating System Commands
# 133 is the Operating System Command 'shell integration'
# ; is a delimiter
# A is start prompt
# B is end prompt
# C is command output start
# \e\\ is the string terminator
# \] ends the enclosure within which characters produce no visible output
#
###
# Show chroot if used: ${debian_chroot:+($debian_chroot)}
# debian_chroot is a local variable that is set earlier in bashrc
# ${parameter:+word}
# If parameter is set, expand to word
# If parameter is unset or empty, expands to an empty string
# Here, surround the value of $debian_chroot with () if it is set
# Otherwise, omit
#
###
# Set text rendering to bold + green foreground: \[\033[01;32m\]
# \[ start of enclosure of non-printing characters
# \033[ is the Command Sequence Indicator prefix
# 01;32 is two parameter bytes: 1 for bold, 32 for color foreground gren
# m is the final byte for Select Graphic Rendition
# \] ends the enclosure of non-printing characters
#
###
# user@host
# \u@\h
#
###
# Clear formatting: \[033[00m\]
# \[ starts non-printing enclosure
# 033[ is the Command Sequence Identifier Prefix
# 00m resets text rendering
# \] closes non-printing enclosure
#
###
# Colon
# : (just that)
#
###
# Set text rendering to bold and blue: \[\033[01;34m\]
# \[
# \033[
# 01;34
# m
# \]
#
###
# Current working directory, with $HOME as ~
# \w
#
###
# Clear formatting: \[0033[00m\]
# \[ starts non-printing enclosure
# 033[ is the Command Sequence Identifier Prefix
# 00m resets text rendering
# \] closes non-printing enclosure
#
###
# Prompt indicator: \$
# \$ is '$' for non-root users and '#' for root users
#
###
# Prompt end: \[\e]133;B\e\\\]
# \[ starts an enclosure within which characters produce no visible output
# \e] is an escape character for Operating System Commands
# 133 is the Operating System Command 'shell integration'
# ; is a delimiter
# A is start prompt
# B is end prompt
# C is command output start
# \e\\ is the string terminator
# \] ends the enclosure within which characters produce no visible output
#
# Right-justified time/date: \[\033[s\033[${COLUMNS}\033[19D\]\D{%Y-%m-%d %T}\[\033[u\]
# Non-printing sequence begin: \[
# Save cursor position: \033[s
# Move cursor right: \033[${COLUMNS}C
# Move cursor left: \033[19D
# Non-printing sequence end: \]
# Date/time stamp: \D{%Y-%m-%d %T}
# Non-printing sequence begin: \[
# Restore cursor position: \033[u
# Non-printing sequence end: \]
#
# COLUMNS is an environment variable

